These two binaries are only used by the "put this AP's original firmware back"
path in `arista-field.py`, when the RAM installer image has no mtd tools of its
own.

- `flash_erase`, `nandwrite`: from mtd-utils 2.3.1, licence GPL-2.0.
- Built for aarch64 / musl with the OpenWrt toolchain (ipq807x, Cortex-A53).
- Source: mtd-utils 2.3.1 from <https://git.infradead.org/mtd-utils.git>,
  built unmodified by this project's OpenWrt build tree. The corresponding
  source is available on request: open an issue in this repository.
